  "gaps": [
    "Open electives range from 30 to 42 credit hours; the ledger assumes no optional concentration (42). If one of the optional 12-credit concentrations is completed, open electives drop to 30.",
    "The concentration courses (Arson Investigation, Communication, Criminology, Forensic Psychology, Forensics, Human Services, and Public Safety Health and Wellness) are optional and not included. The Human Services and Public Safety Health and Wellness concentrations are listed as not currently available for enrollment.",
    "PSY 1301 is required within Social and Behavioral Sciences. Its title and credit hours are not printed in the capture.",
    "The capture lists course options only for Humanities and Fine Arts Groups A and B, and Group B may be truncated. Approved course lists for Social and Behavioral Sciences, Natural Sciences, Mathematics, History, and English Composition are not in the capture.",
    "The capture mentions 'degree program upper-level requirements', but the number of upper-level credits required is not stated.",
    "No residency or institutional credit requirement (minimum credits that must be completed at Columbia Southern University) is stated in the capture.",
    "Transfer credit limits and minimum grade/GPA requirements are not stated in the capture."
